THE GREEN CITY PROJECT
A city becomes sustainable when residents, planners, and businesses work together. Urban trees reduce heat, absorb carbon dioxide, and provide habitats for birds. Public transport can reduce traffic congestion when it is reliable, affordable, and accessible. Rainwater harvesting helps communities conserve water during dry seasons. The project proposes planting native trees, improving cycle paths, and creating neighbourhood gardens. Success will be measured through tree survival rates, public transport use, water saved, and resident participation.